# Always push + TEST pull

When a fix or small change is ready to ship (unless the user explicitly says not to, or is mid-feature on a named branch they want kept open):

1. Commit with a clear message
2. Push to `origin/main` (or merge the feature branch into `main` and push)
3. End with a ready-to-paste **TEST** deploy command per `pull-after-push.mdc` / `deploy-commands.mdc` — never production unless asked

Default to TEST only. Choose full vs quick deploy as those rules specify.
